*~
.DS_Store
# Phase 11 cleanup (2026-10-26): a wildcard, not an enumerated list of
# known variants — any future .env.* file (local/staging/testing/...)
# is excluded by default instead of only the ones already named here.
# .env.example is the one deliberate exception: it has no real secrets
# and must stay tracked as the template new clones copy from.
.env*
!.env.example
# WAFFRLI (2026-11-05): Docker template, no secrets (secrets are generated locally by scripts/setup.*)
!.env.docker.example
# Phase 11G (2026-10-26): a distribution/review archive of this project
# (e.g. a zip handed to an external reviewer) is exactly the kind of
# thing that silently carries a real .env with it if built carelessly —
# found a real one (base.zip, untracked but present on disk, containing
# a genuine .env) during this phase's own review. Ignored outright so
# one can never be accidentally `git add`ed; building a distributable
# archive should exclude .env deliberately (see starter:new's own
# exclusion list for the pattern to follow), never rely on this alone.
*.zip
.phpactor.json
.phpunit.result.cache
/.fleet
/.idea
/.nova
/.phpunit.cache
/.vscode
/.zed
/auth.json
/node_modules
/public/build
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db
/public/vendor/scalar
/backups
/e2e/.env
/e2e/results
